  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirements\nThe task had two components:\n1. **Convert 15 kg of sulfuric acid to moles**\n2. **Display the percentage composition of H, S, and O by weight**\n\n## Screenshot Evidence\n\n**Screenshots 1-3 (WolframAlpha query \"15 kg sulfuric acid to moles\"):**\n- Input interpretation: \"convert 15 kg of sulfuric acid to moles\"\n- Result: **153 mol (moles)** ✓\n- The first screenshot also shows \"Mass composition for 15 kg\": H (hydrogen) 0.308 kg (2.1%), O (oxygen) 9.788 kg (65.2%), S (sulfur) 4.904 kg (32.7%)\n\n**Screenshots 4-5 (WolframAlpha query \"percent composition of sulfuric acid\"):**\n- Result table shows mass percent: **H (hydrogen) 2.056%, O (oxygen) 65.25%, S (sulfur) 32.69%** ✓\n- A mass fraction pie chart is also displayed\n\n## Response Verification\nThe result response states:\n- \"15 kg of sulfuric acid = approximately 153 mol\" — matches the screenshot result of 153 mol ✓\n- \"Percentage composition by weight: H ~2.06% (2.056%), S ~32.69%, O ~65.25%\" — matches the mass percent values in the screenshots exactly ✓\n- The molar mass of 98.07 g/mol mentioned in the response is consistent with the values shown (not contradicted by screenshots)\n\n## Mathematical Sanity Check\n- 15,000 g ÷ 98.07 g/mol ≈ 153 mol ✓\n- H: (2 × 1.008)/98.07 ≈ 2.056% ✓\n- S: 32.06/98.07 ≈ 32.69% ✓\n- O: (4 × 16.00)/98.07 ≈ 65.25% ✓\n\n## Conclusion\nBoth parts of the task were completed successfully. The conversion to moles (153 mol) was performed and displayed, and the percentage composition by weight for all three elements (H, S, O) was obtained and reported accurately, consistent with the screenshots.\n\n**Verdict: SUCCESS**",
